# Curated artefact -- Phase 3b, M1, first native QNX boot on the Jetson Orin Nano (2026-09-10).
# Captured live over the J14 debug header (TCU, UART2_TXD pin 4) with an FT232R adapter at 115200 8N1.
# Sequence: Linux shutdown -> kexec -> t234 shim (EL2) -> startup-t234-orin-nano -> procnto.
# RESULT: the QNX kernel ran. startup, MMU, GICv3 re-init against a Linux-used GIC, the qtime timer,
# the TCU console callouts and the syspage all came up, and procnto printed 'T234 M1: procnto up'.
# User space then failed on two buildfile errors, not kernel errors: the runtime linker ldqnx-64.so.2
# was a dangling symlink (errno 83, ELIBACC) and devc-pty sat outside PATH (errno 2, ENOENT).
# The em-dash in one startup message renders as ??? on this console; cosmetic, fixed afterwards.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

